Vita (--vita-fast-reg-repeats=off|on|verify, platform/vita/runtime/fast_painter.hpp): register
loads that reach their handlers although they change nothing. The register census counted, per frame in Kakariko, 7,900 BP writes decoded of
which 1,600 were needed by the next draw, and 2,100 light loads of which 4 % carried new values.
- BP 0xE0-0xE7 hold a TEV colour register or a konst colour (bit 23 of the value says which). The
  BP shadow keeps one value per address; J3D sends the colour and the konst of an address with
  every material, so each write differs from the other kind's and is decoded again. The last
  decoded value is now kept per address and kind.
- Light loads (XF 0x600-0x67F) are decoded and compared field by field. The raw words last decoded
  are now kept and compared first.
On: a write equal to the kept value does not go to its handler (for BP the shadow, its valid bit
and the uniform flag are set as the handler would set them). Verify: the handler still runs and
the colour registers, konst colours or lights are compared before and after. Off by default.

